{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And your words will be verified, and you will not die.</b> Meaning, that if they do not do this he will declare that you are spies, and therefore they cannot leave one of their number behind, for he will surely die, and they have no authority to do so — rather they would all be killed, and so forth; and from now on they would be liable to death for being spies. Or it may mean that they will not die of hunger, for he will deal well with them by providing them sustenance — and this is what they said to their father (Genesis 42:34): ״וְאֶת הָאָרֶץ תִּסְחָרוּ״."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:48:02.440226757Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}